1. Introduction
This project is a Contact Book that runs in the terminal. It stores a name, phone number, email address and postal address for each person and lets the user add, view, edit, delete, list and search these entries. The program is written in Python and uses only the standard library.
The main idea was to build something small but complete: a program with a clear menu, checks on the data the user types in, and storage that survives after the program is closed. The project applies the basics of Python taught in the course, namely functions, dictionaries, conditionals, loops, string handling, file handling and exception handling.
2. Problem Statement
Phone numbers and email addresses are often kept in different places such as notebooks, messages or simply remembered. This makes it slow to find a contact, and mistakes like a wrong number or a repeated entry are easy to make.
The problem is to build a simple contact manager that can run on any computer with Python, accepts only sensible data, and keeps the contacts saved between sessions. The objectives are:
Provide add, view, edit, delete, list and search operations through a simple menu.
Check phone numbers, email addresses and names before saving them.
Save the contacts to a file and load them again when the program starts.
Show clear messages when the user enters something wrong or the file has a problem.
