5. System Architecture
The program follows a simple layered design. The user talks only to the menu. The menu calls the operation functions, which use the validation functions to check input and the in-memory dictionary to hold the contacts. The storage functions copy that dictionary to and from a JSON file.

Figure 1: System architecture of the Contact Book
Presentation layer: display_menu() and the main() loop show the options and read the choice.
Application logic layer: six functions, one for each operation.
Validation layer: is_valid_phone() and is_valid_email() return True or False.
Data layer: the contact_book dictionary is the working copy, and load_contacts() and save_contacts() keep it in sync with contacts.json.
