7. Design Decisions and Rationale
Decision
Reason
Dictionary keyed by name
Lookup, duplicate check and delete are all one step, and it maps directly to a JSON object.
JSON file for storage
Readable, built into Python, and enough for a small contact list. A database would be more than this project needs.
Functions in one file
The program is small, so one file with one function per task keeps it easy to follow.
Phone must be exactly 10 digits
Matches Indian mobile numbers and makes the rule simple to check and explain.
Email check is simple
Checking for "@" and a dot after it catches common typing mistakes without a complicated pattern.
Blank input keeps old value on edit
The user only has to type the field they want to change.
Save after every change
Nothing is lost if the program is closed suddenly.
Damaged file is renamed to .bak
If contacts.json cannot be read, it is kept as a backup so the next save does not overwrite it.
List is sorted by name
Output is always in the same order, which makes it easier to read.

